# --- hermit-ui dashboard ---
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit the real `.env` (it is gitignored).

# Postgres connection string used by Prisma. Required.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/hermit_ui"

# Port the Next.js custom server (server.ts) listens on. Default: 3000.
PORT=4101

# "production" on a server, "development" locally.
NODE_ENV=production

# Shared machine key the gateway presents to the dashboard's /api/sync routes.
# Must match HERMIT_KEY on the gateway. Stored hashed (bcrypt) in the DB; this
# value seeds/verifies a MachineKey row. Leave blank to disable sync auth in dev.
# HERMIT_KEY=

# Display name shown in the UI for the human operator. Optional.
# HERMIT_USER_NAME=

# Where uploaded images and the image cache are written. Optional — sensible
# defaults are used when unset.
# HERMIT_UPLOAD_DIR=
# HERMIT_IMAGE_CACHE_DIR=

# --- push notifications ---
# Three transports, all optional and independent. See docs/no-app-push-design.md.
#
# Bark needs NOTHING here: the device key the user pastes into Settings → Push is
# itself the credential, so that transport works on a bare server.

# Absolute origin used to build notification tap-through URLs. Set it whenever the
# dashboard is not at the default https://dash.swaylab.ai.
#
# On a SECOND deployment driven from another dashboard's installed PWA, point
# this at the PWA's origin, not at this deployment: the tap has to open the app
# the user actually installed. The path already carries `?m=<machineId>`, so the
# app selects this deployment's workspace on the way in.
# PUSH_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://dash.swaylab.ai

# There is deliberately no server-side quiet-hours setting. Every event is
# delivered when it happens, marked urgent or not; iOS Focus modes decide what
# that means at 03:00. See src/server/push/suppress.ts.

# Web Push — notifications to the installed PWA. No Apple Developer account
# needed. Generate the pair once with `npx tsx scripts/gen-vapid-keys.ts`;
# rotating it invalidates every existing subscription. The private key is a
# secret: keep the canonical copy in the `secret` store, never in git.
#
# Deployments that share ONE installed PWA must share ONE VAPID keypair. A push
# subscription is minted against a single public key, and a browser can only
# hold one subscription per service worker — so a second deployment with its own
# keypair stores the device row happily and then has every send rejected by the
# push service. Copy the pair; don't generate a second one.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com

# APNs — the native iOS shell in apps/ios only. Requires a PAID Apple Developer
# account (the aps-environment entitlement). With any of the four missing the
# transport no-ops and logs one line at startup; nothing else breaks.
# APNS_KEY_P8="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIG...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
# APNS_KEY_ID=
# APNS_TEAM_ID=
# APNS_BUNDLE_ID=ai.swaylab.hermit

# ── Driving this deployment from another dashboard's PWA ────────────────────
# An installed PWA is bound to the origin it was installed from. To let that one
# app also drive THIS deployment, list its origin here: the browser sends the
# machine key as the `x-asst-key` header (never a cookie), which makes every
# request non-simple, so it is preflighted and refused without an allowance.
# Comma-separated; empty (the default) means no cross-origin access at all.
# CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS=https://dash.swaylab.ai
